Spec: Explicit owner enrollment and secure grant tooling

Purpose:
  Provision device identities and approve or revoke scoped service grants without giving applications owner authority.

Owns:
  ./LinkGate.Owner.Console.csproj
  ./Program.cs

References:
  ../LinkGate.Broker/SecureIdentity.sdd
  ../LinkGate.Broker/SecureAuthority.sdd

Must:
  Permit certificate-only trust of an access-only peer without inventing an unused dial endpoint, requiring the same explicit public-key confirmation and expected revision.
  Permit explicit command-line declaration approval only with matching pending revision, decision version and owner-confirmed canonical manifest hash; expose original review-operation lookup.
  Dispatch server-owner commands only to the explicit mTLS owner entry, preserving existing local commands and their authority boundary.
  Offer local visitor access request inspection, proposal export, explicit approval, bounded grant inspection and versioned revocation with retained operation UUIDs.
  Create keys only in private owner/device directories and transfer only CSR, public certificate and public root files.
  Require explicit retained operation UUIDs and expected revisions for authority mutations.
  Export a grant proposal before approval and reject stale proposal versions during activation.
  Preserve existing identities, never overwrite secret files and keep all private keys out of output.
  Leave application declaration review to the separate host-only review workflow.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify request, issuance, installation, peer trust, retained outcome lookup and revocation in isolated CLI acceptance.
